{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 5,
  "simulation_id": "sim-01",
  "member_id": "olsson-eva",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B043",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and pioneering realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B002",
    "B020"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration has changed from B002 to B043. Optical lattice clocks present a sharply delimited physical invention: the magic-wavelength principle permits confinement of many atoms while preserving the clock transition, and pioneering realization produced an experimentally reproducible new measurement capability. This is not recognition for incremental clock performance or prospective redefinition of time, but for the original instrument concept and defining experimental work that opened precision tests otherwise inaccessible. Katori and Ye are the proposed conceptual and experimental credit, subject to final historical confirmation. Compared with B002, B043 more securely meets the requirement that the recognized achievement itself, rather than its subsequent technological deployment, be a Nobel-scale advance in physics.",
    "case_against": "The historical record must still distinguish the founding lattice-clock principle and pioneering realizations from contributions of other early optical-clock researchers and later international metrology advances. A two-person attribution is defensible only if that review confirms that Katori and Ye capture the indispensable original conceptual and experimental contributions. The achievement is an instrument platform, so the citation should remain narrowly tied to the invention and pioneering realization rather than undifferentiated later performance improvements.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that the magic-wavelength concept and decisive experimental work made optical lattice clocks an independently replicated capability, while requiring a boundary between the foundational architecture and later performance gains.",
        "response": "I agree, and this distinction resolves my principal round-1 hesitation. The relevant merit is the original physical means of interrogating an ensemble without the usual trapping shift, demonstrated in a durable measurement regime; replication establishes maturity but does not substitute for the invention. The historical review should test the proposed attribution against that narrow boundary before a final award."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson maintains that Nd-Fe-B magnets are a compactly attributable, decades-proven materials discovery with exceptional practical consequence, while acknowledging the question whether they are sufficiently centered on fundamental physics.",
        "response": "I continue to regard B002 as a serious alternative, particularly because Sagawa and Croat may represent distinct original invention paths and the materials achievement has been tested at immense scale. But the unresolved distinction between an extraordinary industrial materials development and a physics-prize discovery is decisive in this comparison. B043 has a more direct and self-contained physical principle, experimental realization, and fundamental-measurement reach."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson argues that B020 created direct empirical access to black-hole shadows, but accepts that the proposed three-person attribution must be rigorously justified against the collaborative character of the Event Horizon Telescope.",
        "response": "The observation is a landmark and remains my leading observational alternative. Yet the individual causal roles required for a three-person award are structurally more difficult to delimit in such a broad collaboration. For B043, the proposed pair maps more directly onto a specified principle and its defining realization, provided the early optical-clock historical record confirms that mapping."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether primary historical evidence confirms that Katori and Ye alone delimit the indispensable founding concept and pioneering experimental realization of optical lattice clocks.",
      "Where the citation should draw the boundary between the original lattice-clock invention and later advances in systematic control, performance, and applications.",
      "Whether archival evidence can establish both the relative priority of Croat and Sagawa and a Nobel-scale physical formulation of B002 independent of industrial deployment."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No connection to the credited candidates is apparent from the supplied profile. Göran Johansson is a Chalmers Physics colleague but is not a candidate; this does not itself indicate a recusal issue."
  }
}
